			<div class="content" id="post-content-1965012">
									

<p>Must give thanks and credits to users Huitzil, Morrte, and Zolgamax</p>
<p>The first two were largely responsible for most of the better changelog entries and staying up past midnight, and the group as a whole for making it less stupid and more interesting</p>
<p>Prolly time for some of the stupid references I made</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers!?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>- The whole thing started as a potential rewrite of <a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-664">SCP-664</a> and changed substantially since Anaxagoras claimed the rewrite first.</p>
<p>- Agents <a href="http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0922035/">West</a> and <a href="http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0682495/">Pierce</a> are &quot;The Wire&quot; references, back when there was a lot more dialogue before Expedition-017</p>
<p>- The &quot;bugbears&quot; are originally from my failed dinosaur SCP thing, old SCP-1693 &quot;Refugees&quot;. Despite the weakness of that SCP, people loved the bugbears, called such because they are ursine creatures with insect-like faces and chitin.</p>
<p>- &quot;Silos&quot; reference from <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3RGpO4h436c">C&amp;C Red Alert</a></p>
<p>- &quot;Cone&quot; is a synonym for <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C5e6eG6bXAQ">Pylon...</a></p>
<p>- Reference to Tartessian users meant to accentuate that people from different time periods/universes were getting in. <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nantucket_series">Tartessians in the continental US...?</a></p>
<p>- Garnishes and sediment were unintentional Portal references I only realized after putting them in</p>
<p>- <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EpilepticTrees">Epileptic trees</a></p>
</div>
